1
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:22,105
Did the association get
this year's donation?

3
00:00:22,605 --> 00:00:23,940
They did, sir.

4
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:28,778
2026 NATIONAL SPORTS FESTIVAL
HIGH SCHOOL TEAM LINEUP

5
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:34,159
COACH: HONG DO-YEOP
ASSISTANT COACH: JANG TAE-HA

6
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:38,371
Hong Do-yeop.

7
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:40,498
Jang Tae-ha.

8
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,501
They're together?

9
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:51,843
So the man who despised anyone
who fought outside the ring

10
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:55,555
took back his precious disciple.

11
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:58,682
The pride of Gujin, Kim Pil-seung!

12
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:00,518
You've got this!

13
00:01:12,822 --> 00:01:14,032
He's got this.

14
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,660
That's not what she should be doing
right about now.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,211
Before I lost my memory,

16
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:28,171
maybe I was a pro…

17
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:30,965
A prodigy!

18
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:33,760
- You <i>were</i> amazing.
- You're smart.

19
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:36,596
She lost her memory?

20
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:41,267
We found her location.

21
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:44,979
It's said that she lives in Gujin
with Jang Tae-ha.

22
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:48,775
I need to see for myself.

23
00:02:11,089 --> 00:02:12,507
Is this yours, sir?

24
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:37,991
Thank you.

25
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:40,743
No problem.

26
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:48,376
But

27
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:51,129
is that really yours?

28
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:54,883
It looks like a woman's watch.

29
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:05,267
Does it?

30
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:07,145
You have a keen eye.

31
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:10,148
It's clearly too small for your wrist.

32
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:14,319
It used to be a woman's…

33
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:17,906
but now it's mine.

34
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,494
Okay.

35
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,168
I'll see you again.

36
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,053
What's wrong with me?

37
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:43,348
It's not even cold, but I have the chills.

38
00:03:57,695 --> 00:04:01,573
The thing is, I've never seen him
around the village before.

39
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:04,117
He was wearing
a really nice and expensive suit

40
00:04:04,118 --> 00:04:07,538
and had a full head of hair
and these super intense eyes.

41
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:11,584
But what's weird is
he had a woman's watch.

42
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:14,045
- Do you know who he is?
- I sure do.

43
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:15,879
Who is he?

44
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,839
What do you think it means

45
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:21,135
when a man with intense eyes goes around
wearing a woman's watch?

46
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:24,389
It means he's lost his marbles.

47
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,647
You're here, Song-wol.

48
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:37,609
PAYCHECK

49
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:39,862
What's this? "Paycheck"?

50
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:45,660
Wait, I get paid?

51
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,829
Yay me!

52
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,667
It's cute, my paycheck.

53
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:57,714
Now that you got paid,
why not buy yourself some new clothes?

54
00:04:58,214 --> 00:05:01,884
You like to dress up, don't you?

55
00:05:13,271 --> 00:05:14,438
So,

56
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:19,651
you're saying that you're Baek Sang-gil,
Chairman of Mirae Eden.

57
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:23,322
But why did you come to see me?

58
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:25,283
If you don't mind me asking.

59
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:29,078
Why did you meet Gwak Chi-hyeon, Doctor?

60
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:32,873
Prosecutor Go… I mean, Go Ji-won

61
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,918
was an amnesia patient
who came to see me about a month ago.

62
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:39,504
She was suspicious
of her current boyfriend,

63
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:42,799
and one day, she said she remembered
a man named Gwak Chi-hyeon.

64
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,594
She wanted to know the truth,

65
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:49,557
so I tracked him down and met with him.

66
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:54,812
Then why did you tell Gwak Chi-hyeon
that you didn't know Prosecutor Go?

67
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:03,112
I was scared.

68
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:07,199
It seems as though
something big is going on,

69
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,368
and I'd rather not get involved.

70
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:12,872
I'm just a regular doctor
who runs a small clinic in the country.

71
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:16,417
I really don't know anything.

72
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:22,382
So I would be very grateful
if you could please leave now.

73
00:06:28,846 --> 00:06:31,516
When do you think
Prosecutor Go will get her memory back?

74
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:34,726
That's impossible to know.

75
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:35,853
Aren't you her doctor?

76
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:38,231
I'm her doctor, yes. Not a fortune…

77
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:42,610
I'm sorry. That came out a bit…

78
00:06:54,414 --> 00:06:56,582
There must be a way
to get her memory back quicker,

79
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,335
mustn't there?

80
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:19,814
Tae-ha.

81
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,292
Hands off.

82
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,438
You can kill me, sir.

83
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,606
You don't have to kill me nicely.

84
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:48,986
You can do whatever you want to me
until your anger is gone.

85
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:53,115
Please…

86
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,956
Please just spare Prosecutor Go's life.

87
00:09:03,251 --> 00:09:05,085
She doesn't have her memory right now.

88
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:07,380
She doesn't even know
that she was a prosecutor.

89
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,216
She can't do you any harm, sir.

90
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:15,555
Tae-ha.

91
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:19,642
Yes?

92
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:23,437
Enough with the melodrama.

93
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:31,320
Why did you let her live?

94
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,497
She's someone I owed from a long time ago.

95
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:58,598
The Jang Tae-ha, who worked like a machine
for 14 years without a single slipup,

96
00:09:59,932 --> 00:10:03,144
did all this because of
some petty sentiment?

97
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:30,838
Come with me.

98
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:59,450
Say hi to your boys. It's been a while.

99
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:12,296
Had they served you well,

100
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:15,424
you never would have made
the wrong choice.

101
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,134
Such a shame.

102
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,011
No!

103
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:24,600
Sir!

104
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:28,896
Jang Tae-ha, don't move!

105
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:36,779
The boys are to blame for that.

106
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,324
Please stop!

107
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:42,451
Sir!

108
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:44,828
Hurt me instead!

109
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:47,206
Come on, that's not right.

110
00:11:47,832 --> 00:11:49,999
You know how fond I was of you.

111
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,378
I'd never do something
this childish to you.

112
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:54,630
Sir!

113
00:11:56,549 --> 00:11:58,300
No, don't!

114
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:00,385
Tae-ha, sir!

115
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,303
Sir!

116
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:05,683
Tae-ha!

117
00:12:45,806 --> 00:12:48,142
Throughout both Eastern
and Western history,

118
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:52,855
people didn't use guns or knives
to torture the worst of them.

119
00:12:58,319 --> 00:13:01,405
Instead, they covered their eyes
with a single black cloth.

120
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:06,535
The fear of not knowing what will happen
is scarier than any gun or knife.

121
00:13:08,954 --> 00:13:10,538
I know what you're planning.

122
00:13:10,539 --> 00:13:12,540
Go on and try.

123
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:17,463
But every day, your imagination will
eat away at you, wondering about my plan…

124
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:20,549
for you…

125
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,845
and Prosecutor Go.

126
00:13:30,684 --> 00:13:33,354
Escort Director Jang home,

127
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:35,689
respectfully.

128
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:50,370
Jang Tae-ha seems unaware of the extra
evidence Gwak Chi-hyeon mentioned.

129
00:13:50,371 --> 00:13:54,458
If he had it, he wouldn't have begged.
He would have tried to negotiate.

130
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:02,341
Only Prosecutor Go knows
where that evidence is.

131
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,178
But she can't remember.

132
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:09,013
If we just take care of her now--

133
00:14:09,014 --> 00:14:13,310
No. That bitch, Prosecutor Go,
must have had a plan B.

134
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:20,859
If it's buried somewhere
and manages to surface somehow,

135
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,902
it'll be the end for me and Mayor Ju.

136
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:24,321
We must find and destroy it.

137
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:28,742
In order to do that…

138
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:36,667
we have to stir Prosecutor Go's memory.

139
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:40,796
Hey, Tae-ha.

140
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:44,632
Tae-ha, what did you mean by that?

141
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:45,925
Baek Sang-gil was here?

142
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,219
Did you meet him?

143
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,931
Is Eun-sae okay?

144
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:53,934
I have to go somewhere now.

145
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:56,979
I'll tell you the details when I get back.

146
00:14:57,479 --> 00:14:59,355
Please protect Eun-sae while I'm gone.

147
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:00,649
- Okay.
- Of course.

148
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:09,575
Goodness.

149
00:15:14,663 --> 00:15:15,623
Jang Tae-ha.

150
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:19,001
Gi-jun, I need your help.

151
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:24,005
No, I don't want to. I won't.

152
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:28,718
I really don't want to be involved
in this anymore.

153
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:29,887
Go Eun-sae has amnesia.

154
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:33,641
Now's the best time to deal with her
before her memory returns.

155
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:37,353
And yet, Baek Sang-gil kept her alive.
Why do you think that is?

156
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:39,812
How would I know?

157
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,649
I'm asking because I have a hunch.

158
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:43,816
You meeting Gwak Chi-hyeon.

159
00:15:43,817 --> 00:15:45,151
What about that?

160
00:15:45,152 --> 00:15:47,487
I made sure Gwak Chi-hyeon
couldn't make a move.

161
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:49,907
But he was wandering around,
searching for Go Eun-sae.

162
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:53,576
That means Baek Sang-gil
still has a use for him.

163
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:55,995
He must need something more
from Go Eun-sae.

164
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:57,581
We need to find out what that is.

165
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:00,376
Gi-jun, please.

166
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,252
You're my only hope.

167
00:16:04,254 --> 00:16:07,633
I really don't want to. You…

168
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:12,429
We're not close, so you must not know,
but I'm a huge scaredy-cat.

169
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:15,556
I can't watch <i>Unanswered Questions.</i>
It freaks me out.

170
00:16:15,557 --> 00:16:18,893
What's that show called?
<i>Surprise Mystery TV: Truth or Fiction?</i>

171
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:21,855
I can't watch it
because it makes my heart race.

172
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:24,858
Gi-jun, please help me.

173
00:16:26,151 --> 00:16:27,027
I said I won't--

174
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,321
What…

175
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:31,864
Su-ji.

176
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:33,700
I left something behind.

177
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:35,411
This day's driving me crazy.

178
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:39,415
What does Jang Tae-ha want you
to help him with?

179
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:41,083
What?

180
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:50,174
Okay, fine.

181
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:55,222
Let's hear what it is
you want me to help you with.

182
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:56,890
What is it?

183
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:05,941
CHEONAN SAMGEORI REST STOP

184
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:28,714
What did he say? Did you find out?

185
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:33,760
<i>When do you think
Prosecutor Go will get her memory back?</i>

186
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:37,139
Why would Chairman Baek Sang-gil…

187
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:39,516
Why would he come to you…

188
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,730
To be honest,

189
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:49,275
I prefer to stay out of messy affairs,
so I played dumb.

190
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:51,903
But since the chairman himself

191
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:54,281
came all the way
to ask me about Go Ji-won,

192
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:57,201
I think it's time I knew
what's going down.

193
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:02,831
What does Chairman Baek want
from Prosecutor Go?

194
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:07,043
Why would I tell you that?

195
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:08,921
How could I trust you?

196
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,843
<i>I made sure Gwak Chi-hyeon
couldn't make a move.</i>

197
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:17,971
I heard you almost died.

198
00:18:19,014 --> 00:18:20,390
Please, no!

199
00:18:22,142 --> 00:18:22,976
No!

200
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:31,235
Wait. How do you even know about that?

201
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,070
Chairman Baek told me.

202
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:41,494
I'm sure you know very well

203
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:43,121
that for people like us,

204
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:46,291
the moment we are rendered useless,
we're done.

205
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:50,169
But now that the chairman
has actually found Go Ji-won,

206
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:53,005
we need to be of help to him in some way

207
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:55,008
in order for us both to live.

208
00:18:55,884 --> 00:18:56,802
Don't you think?

209
00:19:00,472 --> 00:19:02,432
Let's find it together.

210
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,643
How we can be of help.

211
00:19:06,478 --> 00:19:07,729
What is it

212
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:11,900
that the chairman wants
from Prosecutor Go?

213
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:15,444
Chairman Baek Sang-gil
and Mayor Ju Min-jong.

214
00:19:15,445 --> 00:19:18,031
There's another piece of evidence
linking them.

215
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,036
Never make me do this again.

216
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:27,833
It was no easy feat, you know.

217
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:31,460
He's not exactly the talkative type.

218
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:35,506
But since I'm a psychiatrist
and I understand human psychology,

219
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:37,842
I have a way with words.

220
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:42,598
You should know
that I got him to talk on pure skill.

221
00:19:43,098 --> 00:19:44,515
Yeah, thanks.

222
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:46,226
Hey, I'm not done.

223
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,981
Would it be okay
if I heard you out another time?

224
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:53,275
No, it's not that.

225
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:56,069
This.

226
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:02,451
I bought this on my way to Seoul.

227
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:08,248
It's the latest model
that detects all wiretaps and GPS devices.

228
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:12,419
What if Baek Sang-gil planted something
while watching you?

229
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,881
I also bought one and checked,
but there was nothing, at least in my car.

230
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:20,552
And still, I'm whispering like this.
You always have to be vigilant.

231
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:29,561
Thanks, Gi-jun.
I'll make sure to repay you for your help.

232
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:31,104
Don't mention it.

233
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:41,531
Guess I'm pretty damn cool too.

234
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:50,581
What? Information
about the stowaway boat plan leaked?

235
00:20:50,582 --> 00:20:54,169
It seems so. I lost contact
with one of the Japanese brokers.

236
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:56,421
<i>I know what you're planning.</i>

237
00:20:57,005 --> 00:20:58,590
Go on and try.

238
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:04,178
Can we arrange another date?

239
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:06,056
<i>Not unless we want a serious delay.</i>

240
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:09,601
Can you at least change the time
the boat leaves that day?

241
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:11,519
I'm relying on you, Kaito.

242
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:14,231
Just like in Namba, Osaka, ten years ago.

243
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:22,281
There's nothing in our gym.

244
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:28,160
Baek Sang-gil never leaves loose ends.

245
00:21:28,161 --> 00:21:30,079
Now that he knows there's more evidence,

246
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:33,166
he won't kill Go Eun-sae
until he finds and destroys it.

247
00:21:34,584 --> 00:21:37,421
In a way, it's lucky she lost her memory.

248
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:41,550
The best move is to smuggle her out
as soon as possible.

249
00:21:42,342 --> 00:21:45,637
We need to send Go Eun-sae away
this Thursday, no matter what.

250
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:47,639
And you?

251
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:49,850
Will you be okay?

252
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:52,894
Yes.

253
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:56,522
Baek Sang-gil will think
there's a chance I have the evidence,

254
00:21:56,523 --> 00:21:58,608
so he won't do anything rash.

255
00:22:02,821 --> 00:22:03,655
I'll be going now.

256
00:22:04,906 --> 00:22:05,824
Okay.

257
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:07,409
Go on.

258
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:16,418
What do we do?

259
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:18,627
Will Tae-ha really be okay?

260
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:20,171
He's not a fool.

261
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:23,592
I'm sure he's already got a plan
in that head of his.

262
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:28,721
How will he ever send Eun-sae away?

263
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:32,516
And how will Eun-sae go on without Tae-ha?

264
00:22:32,517 --> 00:22:36,188
Yeah, it's not like people can control
how they feel.

265
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:39,107
How do you break a bond
that's grown so deep?

266
00:22:45,614 --> 00:22:46,530
Here!

267
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:47,699
My paycheck got this.

268
00:22:49,826 --> 00:22:52,370
It was my first paycheck
after losing my memory.

269
00:22:52,371 --> 00:22:55,123
And I was thinking, "What should I buy?"

270
00:22:55,624 --> 00:23:00,379
People say, if nothing else,
that good shoes are a must.

271
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:03,340
You should have treated yourself.

272
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:07,427
I already have everything I want.

273
00:23:11,515 --> 00:23:14,476
No matter how much I think about it,
all I need is Jang Tae-ha.

274
00:23:19,439 --> 00:23:21,108
What's with that face?

275
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:25,444
Is it because of that superstition

276
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:27,989
that if you give someone shoes,
they'll run away?

277
00:23:29,282 --> 00:23:31,785
I gave them to you
with a different meaning.

278
00:23:37,874 --> 00:23:40,419
From now on, let's walk together.

279
00:23:45,173 --> 00:23:48,677
So, from now on,
no need to try so hard on your own.

280
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:50,762
Let's do everything together.

281
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:56,226
Speaking of which…

282
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:11,116
Put it towards your grandma's meds.

283
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:15,370
Go Eun-sae.

284
00:24:22,711 --> 00:24:23,920
You're touched.

285
00:24:26,715 --> 00:24:30,302
Well, I guess
I just like Jang Tae-ha that much.

286
00:24:59,706 --> 00:25:02,209
<i>From now on, let's walk together.</i>

287
00:25:26,274 --> 00:25:28,068
I looked into what you asked me to.

288
00:25:28,693 --> 00:25:29,528
It's possible.

289
00:25:30,153 --> 00:25:30,987
Good work.

290
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:34,198
And I just transferred some money
to your account.

291
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:36,284
Send it to the guys who got hurt today.

292
00:25:37,035 --> 00:25:39,704
- Sir, you don't have to--
- They got hurt because of me.

293
00:25:42,040 --> 00:25:44,584
How did you survive that world
with such a soft heart?

294
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:48,797
And how will you ever send her away?

295
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:55,469
She didn't even buy
the clothes she wanted today

296
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:57,055
so she could buy you a present.

297
00:25:59,266 --> 00:26:01,101
You like each other so much.

298
00:26:01,851 --> 00:26:05,313
How will you two live
after you send her away?

299
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:11,695
Speaking of which…

300
00:26:16,491 --> 00:26:18,201
I'm going to need everyone's help.

301
00:26:30,463 --> 00:26:31,840
Are you going somewhere today?

302
00:26:36,636 --> 00:26:37,887
To work.

303
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:49,608
What work?

304
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:52,193
Surely, you're not going
to the gym like that?

305
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:57,365
Jang Tae-ha, wait.

306
00:26:58,575 --> 00:27:00,409
This isn't right.

307
00:27:00,410 --> 00:27:02,911
You're really going to go back
to that life?

308
00:27:02,912 --> 00:27:05,623
I found a hospital
specializing in geriatric cancer care.

309
00:27:05,624 --> 00:27:06,625
For Grandma's surgery.

310
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:10,837
I can't afford the hospital bills
with my salary from the gym.

311
00:27:12,005 --> 00:27:13,298
Still, this is wrong.

312
00:27:14,215 --> 00:27:16,343
How can you go back to being a gangster?

313
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:19,763
Then do you have a better idea?

314
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:24,183
I'll find a way to make money with you.

315
00:27:24,184 --> 00:27:26,519
- Take every job I can--
- You're unidentified.

316
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:45,872
- Isn't that Tae-ha?
- It's Tae-ha and Eun-sae.

317
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:48,208
Tae…

318
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:51,001
What's going on? Something seems off.

319
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,837
Jang Tae-ha!

320
00:28:00,095 --> 00:28:02,639
- I think they had a fight.
- Is she crying?

321
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:06,643
Ladies.

322
00:28:08,311 --> 00:28:09,521
What are you doing?

323
00:28:15,777 --> 00:28:16,945
Nothing at all.

324
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:22,616
Something's going on with them, right?

325
00:28:22,617 --> 00:28:24,785
Something out of the ordinary, right?

326
00:28:24,786 --> 00:28:26,370
Talk.

327
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:28,539
We've all got several decades
under our belts.

328
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:31,376
You think we can't read a room? Tell us!

329
00:28:33,962 --> 00:28:37,257
We've been sensing something
for a few days now.

330
00:28:37,841 --> 00:28:41,428
Strangers have been
creeping into our quiet village.

331
00:28:42,137 --> 00:28:44,722
And on roads only ever used
by a few tractors,

332
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:48,809
we saw a huge, black Mercedes-Benz.

333
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:49,727
Tell us.

334
00:28:49,728 --> 00:28:51,603
What on earth is going on?

335
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:54,190
- Tell us.
- Talk.

336
00:28:54,774 --> 00:28:58,235
- Talk!
- Tell us.

337
00:28:58,236 --> 00:28:59,654
Tell us.

338
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:04,325
A prosecutor from Seoul?

339
00:29:07,495 --> 00:29:08,663
Then this whole thing

340
00:29:09,622 --> 00:29:13,126
was an act to save our Eun-sae,
who has no memory?

341
00:29:14,169 --> 00:29:18,214
I'm telling you this knowing
that Tae-ha will beat me to death.

342
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:23,470
Because I think we could also use help
from you S.E.S ladies.

343
00:29:25,054 --> 00:29:27,056
- Okay.
- Goodness.

344
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:31,686
HONG'S BOXING GYM

345
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:34,521
Please help me, Mr. Hong.

346
00:29:34,522 --> 00:29:38,150
Jang Tae-ha listens to you.

347
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:41,028
So please persuade him. Please?

348
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:42,237
It's no use.

349
00:29:42,238 --> 00:29:45,616
Mr. Hong has already tried everything
to stop him.

350
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:47,786
But you know he's as stubborn as a mule.

351
00:29:50,121 --> 00:29:51,372
That darned punk.

352
00:29:56,711 --> 00:29:57,837
What now?

353
00:29:59,297 --> 00:30:02,425
You despise gangsters, Eun-sae.

354
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:09,307
I can't believe it.

355
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:16,731
He promised me
that he would never use violence again.

356
00:30:17,565 --> 00:30:20,193
He's not one to break promises.

357
00:30:27,283 --> 00:30:29,410
How could Jang Tae-ha…

358
00:30:38,294 --> 00:30:39,628
Hey, so you're really…

359
00:30:39,629 --> 00:30:42,715
Can you prepare a two-month supply
of medicine for her?

360
00:30:43,633 --> 00:30:46,177
And something to calm her
when she's feeling down.

361
00:30:48,054 --> 00:30:51,099
Do you think doing this will change
how she feels about you?

362
00:30:52,892 --> 00:30:54,601
Go Eun-sae hates gangsters.

363
00:30:54,602 --> 00:30:57,021
Maybe hating me
will make it hurt a little less.

364
00:31:02,068 --> 00:31:03,485
That crazy bastard!

365
00:31:03,486 --> 00:31:07,948
This is why I was so against
Pil-seung boxing.

366
00:31:07,949 --> 00:31:12,370
If all you know is how to fight,
it's easy to go down that path.

367
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:15,622
That's what I'm saying.

368
00:31:15,623 --> 00:31:19,001
I thought that punk
had gotten his act together.

369
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:20,169
But back to being a thug?

370
00:31:21,129 --> 00:31:23,297
He's a lost cause, he is.

371
00:31:23,298 --> 00:31:24,715
Looking back now,

372
00:31:24,716 --> 00:31:27,342
it's a huge relief
you didn't walk down the aisle.

373
00:31:27,343 --> 00:31:28,261
Eun-sae.

374
00:31:29,220 --> 00:31:32,098
That jerk, Tae-ha. Just dump him already!

375
00:31:37,812 --> 00:31:39,731
I should get home.

376
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:00,335
Tae-ha.

377
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:21,564
There must be a way.

378
00:32:22,315 --> 00:32:24,817
Maybe there's nothing we can do right now,

379
00:32:25,818 --> 00:32:26,903
but one day,

380
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,697
I'm sure there will be a way.

381
00:33:02,355 --> 00:33:05,066
I know saving lives is the priority,

382
00:33:06,109 --> 00:33:07,360
but you shouldn't get hurt.

383
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:14,951
You can't underestimate the power of food.

384
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:18,454
You need a full belly to do great things.

385
00:33:25,294 --> 00:33:27,630
All this while, every day,

386
00:33:28,214 --> 00:33:31,175
every moment must have felt like
walking a tightrope

387
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:33,636
with that enormous burden.

388
00:33:38,349 --> 00:33:39,392
Thank you.

389
00:33:40,226 --> 00:33:43,062
As of now, we have no choice
but to send Eun-sae away

390
00:33:43,646 --> 00:33:45,440
if we want to save her, right?

391
00:33:48,735 --> 00:33:49,736
Yes.

392
00:33:55,992 --> 00:33:59,328
And is there anything we can do to help?

393
00:34:31,069 --> 00:34:31,903
Are you okay?

394
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:38,826
I was so startled.

395
00:34:39,327 --> 00:34:41,370
Even so, how could you collapse like that?

396
00:34:41,954 --> 00:34:43,748
You need to learn to protect yourself.

397
00:34:46,709 --> 00:34:49,295
Easy for someone like you to say.

398
00:34:54,759 --> 00:34:55,802
Want me to teach you?

399
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:02,265
First, get into this position.

400
00:35:02,266 --> 00:35:04,560
If someone attacks you head-on,

401
00:35:05,686 --> 00:35:07,897
you just need to turn your body like this.

402
00:35:09,732 --> 00:35:12,944
Just by turning away,
you can avoid a fatal injury.

403
00:35:13,736 --> 00:35:14,654
Let's try it.

404
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:18,116
- That's it.
- Like this?

405
00:35:18,866 --> 00:35:20,952
And if someone attacks you from behind…

406
00:35:21,828 --> 00:35:23,579
Try grabbing me from behind.

407
00:35:26,165 --> 00:35:26,999
Like this?

408
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:28,709
Then…

409
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:30,878
Step on their foot,

410
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:33,547
elbow them in the stomach,

411
00:35:33,548 --> 00:35:35,466
stick your leg out to trip them up…

412
00:35:38,094 --> 00:35:39,137
and run away.

413
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:48,146
Okay, I'll give it a try.

414
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:52,400
When someone attacks me from behind,

415
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:54,527
I step on their foot,

416
00:35:55,027 --> 00:35:57,529
elbow them in the stomach,

417
00:35:57,530 --> 00:35:59,782
stick my leg out to make them fall,

418
00:36:00,283 --> 00:36:01,325
and run away.

419
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:03,161
You're good.

420
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:07,165
That's cool. It really works.

421
00:36:07,874 --> 00:36:09,375
Let me try one more time.

422
00:36:10,334 --> 00:36:11,169
Okay.

423
00:36:13,838 --> 00:36:14,672
And then…

424
00:36:24,307 --> 00:36:26,184
Step on their foot…

425
00:36:33,316 --> 00:36:36,652
It's a little hard to move if you do this.

426
00:36:59,967 --> 00:37:01,719
Jang Tae-ha.

427
00:37:06,599 --> 00:37:07,433
Go Eun-sae.

428
00:37:09,685 --> 00:37:11,687
Don't take it too hard.

429
00:37:14,273 --> 00:37:16,108
If you just keep living…

430
00:37:21,197 --> 00:37:22,698
everything passes.

431
00:37:28,663 --> 00:37:30,289
You just need to stay alive.

432
00:37:35,753 --> 00:37:37,672
What are you talking about?

433
00:37:44,178 --> 00:37:45,471
I'm sorry for startling you.

434
00:37:48,516 --> 00:37:50,268
For hurting you.

435
00:38:01,237 --> 00:38:02,405
The wind's cold.

436
00:38:03,781 --> 00:38:04,824
I'll get you a jacket.

437
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:47,867
THE DAY OF THE ESCAPE

438
00:38:52,163 --> 00:38:54,456
- Looks delicious.
- Right, well…

439
00:38:54,457 --> 00:38:55,665
No particular reason.

440
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:58,836
You just seemed so down because of Tae-ha,

441
00:38:59,712 --> 00:39:01,629
so, to cheer you up,

442
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:05,800
I thought we'd all get together
and share a meal.

443
00:39:05,801 --> 00:39:06,969
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

444
00:39:07,970 --> 00:39:10,263
It's the tofu poke that you like.

445
00:39:10,264 --> 00:39:12,516
I made the tofu myself.

446
00:39:15,061 --> 00:39:15,895
Okay.

447
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:18,272
Thank you so much.

448
00:39:19,273 --> 00:39:20,107
Everyone.

449
00:39:22,651 --> 00:39:23,902
Let's eat, okay?

450
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:26,655
You know,

451
00:39:27,531 --> 00:39:30,658
I didn't see the tag
and accidentally bought a size small.

452
00:39:30,659 --> 00:39:31,785
Pity.

453
00:39:31,786 --> 00:39:33,996
Why don't you just wear it, Eun-sae?

454
00:39:35,623 --> 00:39:36,499
But this is…

455
00:39:37,708 --> 00:39:39,585
And this…

456
00:39:40,086 --> 00:39:42,545
I made this
when I still had my spiritual powers.

457
00:39:42,546 --> 00:39:44,632
Carry it with you. It'll be effective.

458
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:47,009
- Okay.
- That's precious.

459
00:39:48,427 --> 00:39:49,552
Here!

460
00:39:49,553 --> 00:39:52,764
This is lion's mane liquor.

461
00:39:52,765 --> 00:39:53,723
Take it.

462
00:39:53,724 --> 00:39:55,475
But this is…

463
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:57,727
Isn't this your most prized possession?

464
00:39:57,728 --> 00:40:01,481
You can find mushrooms everywhere
if you dig with a hoe.

465
00:40:01,482 --> 00:40:02,899
I can just make more.

466
00:40:02,900 --> 00:40:03,776
But…

467
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:10,449
This much?

468
00:40:11,117 --> 00:40:12,952
Song-wol.

469
00:40:14,412 --> 00:40:16,080
What is all this, everyone?

470
00:40:16,580 --> 00:40:18,791
Are you all giving me gifts

471
00:40:20,376 --> 00:40:21,585
to cheer me up?

472
00:40:28,884 --> 00:40:30,009
TAFFY VILLAGE PHOTO CONTEST

473
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:31,636
- This is us making taffy.
- Right?

474
00:40:31,637 --> 00:40:32,680
Yes, it is.

475
00:40:33,180 --> 00:40:35,683
- Look at this.
- Do you want a picture?

476
00:40:37,101 --> 00:40:37,977
At the karaoke bar.

477
00:40:39,019 --> 00:40:40,103
How pretty.

478
00:40:40,104 --> 00:40:42,857
That's a good one.
You look like an actress.

479
00:40:47,027 --> 00:40:48,112
This is you guys.

480
00:40:50,823 --> 00:40:52,324
What's wrong? We look great.

481
00:40:53,784 --> 00:40:55,953
You and Song-wol look great in this one.

482
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:58,914
- How lovely.
- You look so pretty.

483
00:41:00,416 --> 00:41:04,378
I really love this village.

484
00:41:05,588 --> 00:41:08,047
The scenery is beautiful,

485
00:41:08,048 --> 00:41:10,467
and I love the sweet smell
of boiling taffy.

486
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:11,594
Of course.

487
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:13,053
Right?

488
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:18,433
Being born and raised in Taffy Village,

489
00:41:18,434 --> 00:41:22,605
I learned that relationships
are like sweet taffy.

490
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:27,859
Once you form a bond,
it's not easy to break it.

491
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:28,943
That's right.

492
00:41:28,944 --> 00:41:32,697
And the warmer it gets,
the more it sticks.

493
00:41:32,698 --> 00:41:36,785
Even if you want to spit it out halfway,
it gets so stuck that you can't.

494
00:41:40,372 --> 00:41:41,499
That's why

495
00:41:42,041 --> 00:41:44,502
if it's meant to be, it'll stick.

496
00:41:45,002 --> 00:41:46,670
You're bound to meet again.

497
00:41:51,425 --> 00:41:52,509
When you think about it,

498
00:41:52,510 --> 00:41:55,178
saying that something is like taffy
is a good thing.

499
00:41:55,179 --> 00:41:57,640
I wonder how it came to be used
in a bad way.

500
00:41:59,475 --> 00:42:00,517
Tae-ha.

501
00:42:00,518 --> 00:42:02,227
You're here. Come.

502
00:42:02,228 --> 00:42:03,062
Hey.

503
00:42:05,773 --> 00:42:06,607
We have to go.

504
00:42:08,317 --> 00:42:09,151
Where?

505
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:13,030
I'll tell you on the way.

506
00:42:15,699 --> 00:42:16,534
Go on.

507
00:42:17,785 --> 00:42:20,912
Everyone, choose your photos
and don't forget to save me some.

508
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:22,580
- Sure.
- We'll be back.

509
00:42:22,581 --> 00:42:23,957
- All right.
- Okay.

510
00:42:23,958 --> 00:42:24,792
See you tomorrow.

511
00:42:56,198 --> 00:42:58,450
And we were just starting to get attached.

512
00:43:08,002 --> 00:43:09,253
Oh dear.

513
00:43:14,925 --> 00:43:16,135
We're going for fresh air?

514
00:43:17,511 --> 00:43:20,055
It's been tough lately.
You could use a change of scenery.

515
00:43:26,186 --> 00:43:27,271
You should get changed.

516
00:43:28,105 --> 00:43:30,649
We're going to see the ocean,
so dress warmly.

517
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:41,243
DAEDANG PORT

518
00:43:48,751 --> 00:43:52,087
I think this is the first time
I've been this far from Taffy Village.

519
00:43:55,215 --> 00:43:57,968
We've seen the sea together before,
haven't we?

520
00:43:59,178 --> 00:44:00,012
Yes.

521
00:44:04,141 --> 00:44:05,643
Is something wrong?

522
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:08,771
You haven't looked so good for a while.

523
00:44:09,521 --> 00:44:11,649
If you're tired, we can turn back.

524
00:44:12,983 --> 00:44:13,817
It's fine.

525
00:44:25,537 --> 00:44:27,915
What's wrong? What's going on?

526
00:44:52,398 --> 00:44:53,816
What's going on?

527
00:44:59,446 --> 00:45:00,447
Listen carefully.

528
00:45:00,948 --> 00:45:04,118
Don't come out no matter what,
and follow Gang-rok when he gets here.

529
00:45:04,618 --> 00:45:06,161
What? To where?

530
00:45:07,162 --> 00:45:08,538
Jang Tae-ha.

531
00:45:08,539 --> 00:45:09,540
Where are you…

532
00:45:16,839 --> 00:45:17,840
Get him!

533
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:25,347
Jang Tae-ha!

534
00:45:34,064 --> 00:45:35,065
Open it!

535
00:45:41,572 --> 00:45:44,199
Get on, now! We don't have time!

536
00:45:54,209 --> 00:45:55,836
- Tae-ha.
- Go, now!

537
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:58,630
We need to hurry!

538
00:46:00,632 --> 00:46:01,508
Now!

539
00:46:05,846 --> 00:46:08,140
He'll be right behind us.

540
00:46:09,892 --> 00:46:11,185
Hey, stop them!

541
00:46:40,589 --> 00:46:41,882
What's going on?

542
00:46:42,591 --> 00:46:43,801
Hurry up and explain.

543
00:46:45,093 --> 00:46:47,428
He's trying to save you.

544
00:46:47,429 --> 00:46:49,139
You're going to Japan now.

545
00:46:49,640 --> 00:46:51,390
What on earth are you talking about?

546
00:46:51,391 --> 00:46:52,810
Just go and stay there for now.

547
00:46:53,602 --> 00:46:55,813
That's the only way for you to live.

548
00:46:57,105 --> 00:46:58,232
What about Jang Tae-ha?

549
00:46:59,358 --> 00:47:00,692
Is he coming too?

550
00:47:01,902 --> 00:47:02,903
Yes.

551
00:47:16,875 --> 00:47:17,751
Eun-sae.

552
00:47:19,211 --> 00:47:21,462
Jang Tae-ha's really coming, right?

553
00:47:21,463 --> 00:47:22,339
Of course.

554
00:47:23,006 --> 00:47:26,093
If you just wait in there for a bit,
he'll be here in no time.

555
00:47:29,221 --> 00:47:30,222
Okay.

556
00:47:41,358 --> 00:47:42,358
Gang-rok.

557
00:47:42,359 --> 00:47:44,236
Jang Tae-ha…

558
00:48:16,852 --> 00:48:18,644
I'm Tae-ha's friend, Kaito.

559
00:48:18,645 --> 00:48:20,230
I'll escort you from here.

560
00:48:20,814 --> 00:48:23,150
- Please follow me.
- You can follow him.

561
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:24,735
He's Tae-ha's man.

562
00:48:26,069 --> 00:48:28,780
I'll go to Tae-ha. Kaito.

563
00:48:34,453 --> 00:48:35,829
This way.

564
00:49:05,859 --> 00:49:07,319
We leave in ten minutes.

565
00:49:08,820 --> 00:49:09,655
Sorry?

566
00:49:10,906 --> 00:49:13,283
Then what about Jang Tae-ha?

567
00:49:36,264 --> 00:49:38,809
KAITO
BOARDING COMPLETE

568
00:50:05,085 --> 00:50:08,088
TIMER

569
00:51:16,948 --> 00:51:19,283
No. I don't want to go.

570
00:51:19,284 --> 00:51:21,535
Where would I go without Jang Tae-ha?

571
00:51:21,536 --> 00:51:24,289
Where is Jang Tae-ha? He was badly hurt.

572
00:51:26,958 --> 00:51:29,711
Jang Tae-ha is risking his life
to save you.

573
00:51:30,295 --> 00:51:31,338
Don't mess this up.

574
00:55:12,100 --> 00:55:13,727
How does blood taste after so long?

575
00:55:20,150 --> 00:55:22,277
Jang Tae-ha is Jang Tae-ha after all.

576
00:55:22,986 --> 00:55:24,779
You managed to save Prosecutor Go.

577
00:55:27,824 --> 00:55:31,036
But did you really think
that boat wouldn't have…

578
00:55:34,414 --> 00:55:35,415
my men on it?

579
00:55:49,471 --> 00:55:50,930
I was just playing with you.

580
00:55:52,098 --> 00:55:53,767
A bit of nostalgia.

581
00:55:54,267 --> 00:55:57,854
And I got to see you fight
like your life was on the line.

582
00:56:19,542 --> 00:56:21,878
Can you at least change the time
the boat leaves?

583
00:56:23,046 --> 00:56:24,338
<i>I'm relying on you, Kaito.</i>

584
00:56:24,339 --> 00:56:27,050
Just like in Namba, Osaka, ten years ago.

585
00:56:34,307 --> 00:56:35,642
<i>Is someone listening in?</i>

586
00:56:36,768 --> 00:56:40,271
<i>I think so. I'm thinking of getting a boat
with a modified motor.</i>

587
00:56:40,772 --> 00:56:41,648
<i>That's too risky.</i>

588
00:56:42,232 --> 00:56:44,818
<i>If we go too fast,
the Coast Guard will spot us.</i>

589
00:56:46,194 --> 00:56:47,362
<i>We have to take the risk.</i>

590
00:56:49,072 --> 00:56:50,572
<i>I'll get the boat ready.</i>

591
00:56:50,573 --> 00:56:52,658
<i>And I can distract the Coast Guard.</i>

592
00:56:52,659 --> 00:56:54,993
I looked into what you asked me to.

593
00:56:54,994 --> 00:56:56,246
It's possible.

594
00:56:58,123 --> 00:57:00,124
This boat leaves in three minutes.

595
00:57:00,125 --> 00:57:02,585
We don't have time.
We need to transfer quickly.

596
00:57:13,930 --> 00:57:15,432
TRANSFERRED TO MOTORBOAT
DEPARTING

597
00:57:38,705 --> 00:57:39,539
Chairman, sir.

598
00:57:40,498 --> 00:57:42,625
Prosecutor Go isn't on the cargo ship.

599
00:58:03,146 --> 00:58:05,148
What's happening…

600
00:58:12,447 --> 00:58:14,908
No! Jang Tae-ha!

601
00:58:15,909 --> 00:58:17,076
No!

602
00:58:20,622 --> 00:58:21,956
I'm Prosecutor Go Ji-won.

603
00:58:22,624 --> 00:58:23,917
We meet again, Prosecutor.

604
00:58:49,275 --> 00:58:50,944
OUR STICKY LOVE

605
00:59:37,574 --> 00:59:41,536
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
